// gamebuilder.org's frame block, the page's own part: what follows the Metaverse Engine's stylized
// frame (metaverse-engine/render/shade/stylized-layout.coax, STY_UNIFORM_FLOATS
// floats) in the uniform floats. hud.coax writes these and gpu/hud.coax's shaders read them, so
// both load this file. Loaded after stylized-layout.coax.
//   HUD_U_POINTER  the pointer's x and y in device pixels, how lit its glow is (0 to 1), and how far
//                  the camera has come down to the world (0 the page's views, 1 the world)
//   HUD_U_SHADE    the box of the panel the ground is dimmed behind, device pixels: x, y, width, height
//   HUD_U_PAGE     device pixels a CSS pixel, how much of the character is shown (0 to 1), how far its
//                  body is left out of the view (0 to 1: the eye in its head, first person), one spare
HUD_U_POINTER :: STY_UNIFORM_FLOATS;
HUD_U_SHADE :: STY_UNIFORM_FLOATS + 4;
HUD_U_PAGE :: STY_UNIFORM_FLOATS + 8;
HUD_UNIFORMS :: STY_UNIFORM_FLOATS + 12;
// A scene draw whose first instance is this or more is the character: its vertices come from the
// `skin` and `tris` stores, not the kit's mesh.
HUD_GHOST_AT :: 4096;
// A scene draw whose first instance is this or more (and under HUD_GHOST_AT) is a place of the
// village: an indexed draw over the pack's vertices, its record the instance itself (the records
// after the kit's two).
HUD_PACK_AT :: 2;
HUD_SKIN_FLOATS :: 9;      // a skinned vertex: where it is in the world, its normal, and its livery's colour (black: a ghost)
// A kit vertex whose material is this or more is a picture the page gives (the home page's ring,
// web/ring.coax): the material less this is which, its uv the picture's own. No material of the
// engine's is as high (arch/solid.coax ARCH_M_COUNT).
RG_M_PICTURE :: 64;
